From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 02:44:56 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: hdma: serve the WAN dequeue port on DMA1TX

hdma_port_chan_tbl() served dequeue ports 7..10 and returned NULL for
anything else, so hdma_port_enable(19) - the first step of the WAN port's
ndo_open - returned -EINVAL and the egress channel was never opened.

Add the port-19 row. The WAN port is not just another channel on the same
controller: AVM's cbm_config.c gives its row dma_ctrl = 1, DMA1TX at
0x1a100000 on the GSWIP-R side, where every LAN row carries DMA2TX at
0x1c100000. The vendor names the pair itself in dma/lantiq_dmax.h as
DMA1TX_GSWIP_R_WAN_CBMP19_CLASS15, which is the label used here.

No device-tree work was needed after all: xrx500.dtsi already describes
dma1tx with its own calibration values (desc-in-sram=1, polling-cnt=108,
lab-cnt=2 - none of which DMA2TX uses), status="okay", GIC_SHARED 65. It
has been probing since the DMA controllers landed; nothing had ever asked
it for a channel.

Two range assumptions moved with the table:

  - HDMA_CBM_DEQ_LAST 10 -> 19, so the armed-latch bitmap covers the WAN
    port. The range is no longer dense - 11..18 are never served - which
    costs eight unused bits of a u32 and preserves the "arm once, stay
    armed" property: a port outside the range reads as never-armed and
    would have its channel reopened on every ndo_open, which leaves the
    DQM-to-DMA coupling stale.

  - The CBM probe-tail channel-open loop was a literal 7..10 over dequeue
    port numbers, which could not have expressed a port on a different
    controller. It now walks the same DT-declared dp port list as the
    preconfig loop above it and resolves each port's dequeue number, so
    the WAN channel opens at probe, before the controllers are enabled,
    which is the side of that boundary it has to be on.

CBM_DQM_DESC_PHYS() needed no change - it is per-dequeue-port and
controller-independent, so it serves the WAN port unchanged: deq 19
gives 0x1e54e000. Checked by extracting it and the armed-latch helpers
and running them, with bits 0..3 and 12 set for deq 7,8,9,10,19 and
6/11/20 correctly reading as never-armed.

hdma_port_disable() shares the table, so it follows automatically and the
two cannot disagree about which channels a port owns.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c
index 65cfde734bd9..ef7040600735 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm.c
@@ -721,17 +721,24 @@ static int cbm_xrx500_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	cbm_enable_controllers();
 
 	{
-		int deq;
+		u32 dp_ports[CBM_MAX_DP_PORTS];
+		int n = cbm_dt_dp_ports(dp_ports, ARRAY_SIZE(dp_ports));
+		int i;
 
-		for (deq = 7; deq <= 10; deq++) {
-			int hret = hdma_port_enable(deq);
+		for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+			struct cbm_dp_egress_res res;
+			int hret;
+
+			if (cbm_dp_egress_res_get(dp_ports[i], &res))
+				continue;
 
+			hret = hdma_port_enable((int)res.deq_port);
 			if (hret)
-				dev_warn(dev, "cbm: probe-time hdma_port_enable(%d) = %d (ndo_open will retry)\n",
-					 deq, hret);
+				dev_warn(dev, "cbm: probe-time hdma_port_enable(%u) = %d (ndo_open will retry)\n",
+					 res.deq_port, hret);
 			else
-				pr_info("cbm: DMA2TX ch%d opened at probe-end for deq %d (AVM order)\n",
-					deq - 5, deq);
+				pr_info("cbm: DMA%uTX ch%u opened at probe-end for deq %u (AVM order)\n",
+					res.dma_ctrl, res.dma_chan, res.deq_port);
 		}
 	}
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/dma/hdma.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/dma/hdma.c
index 2f51c020beb5..b57d7372275d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/dma/hdma.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/dma/hdma.c
@@ -1999,6 +1999,23 @@ static const struct port7_chan_desc port10_channels[] = {
 	  .label = "DMA2TX_CBM_P10_CLASS5", .cbm_deq = 10 },
 };
 
+/*
+ * The WAN port (dp 15) egresses via CBM dequeue port 19 on a DIFFERENT
+ * CONTROLLER, not merely a different channel: AVM cbm_config.c's row for
+ * tmu_port 19 carries dma_ctrl = 1 (DMA1TX @ 0x1a100000, on the GSWIP-R side
+ * of the SoC) where every LAN row carries 2 (DMA2TX @ 0x1c100000). The
+ * channel number is 15, and the vendor names the pair in its own header:
+ * DMA1TX_GSWIP_R_WAN_CBMP19_CLASS15 (dma/lantiq_dmax.h).
+ *
+ * The two controllers are not interchangeable - DMA1TX runs desc-in-sram=1,
+ * polling-cnt=108 and lab-cnt=2, none of which DMA2TX uses - but that is a DT
+ * matter and both nodes are already described; nothing here needs to know.
+ */
+static const struct port7_chan_desc port19_channels[] = {
+	{ .cid = DMA1TX, .pid = DMA1TX_PORT, .nid = DMA_CHANNEL_15,
+	  .label = "DMA1TX_GSWIP_R_WAN_CBMP19_CLASS15", .cbm_deq = 19 },
+};
+
 /*
  * hdma_port_chan_tbl — the per-CBM-dequeue-port channel table, or NULL for a
  * dequeue port this driver does not serve. Shared by hdma_port_enable and
@@ -2022,6 +2039,9 @@ static const struct port7_chan_desc *hdma_port_chan_tbl(int port_id, size_t *n)
 	case 10:
 		*n = ARRAY_SIZE(port10_channels);
 		return port10_channels;
+	case 19:
+		*n = ARRAY_SIZE(port19_channels);
+		return port19_channels;
 	default:
 		return NULL;
 	}
@@ -2052,7 +2072,7 @@ static const struct port7_chan_desc *hdma_port_chan_tbl(int port_id, size_t *n)
  * leaves the port pointing at descriptors nothing will refill.
  */
 #define HDMA_CBM_DEQ_FIRST 7
-#define HDMA_CBM_DEQ_LAST  10
+#define HDMA_CBM_DEQ_LAST  19
 
 static u32 g_hdma_deq_armed;
 
